        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Tedrow, Ohio; Emery, Ohio; Hammondsville, Ohio; Dover Township; Fulton County; Ohio; Chicago; Pittsburgh\n- Systems: Ohio Turnpike\n- Organizations: Edison Local School District\n- Concepts: ghost towns; public school districts\n\nFacts:\n- The Ohio Turnpike, officially the James W. Shocknessy Ohio Turnpike, is a 241.26-mile limited-access toll highway in Ohio and serves as a primary corridor to Chicago and Pittsburgh.\n- Tedrow, Ohio, lies less than one mile north of the Ohio Turnpike, but its nearest exit is several miles away.\n- Emery, Ohio, is a ghost town in Dover Township, Fulton County, Ohio, near present-day Tedrow, Ohio.\n- The Edison Local School District is a public school district based in Hammondsville, Ohio, United States.",
